## Describe the bug

Calling `ssrFixStacktrace(error)` where the original stack trace goes through line 1 or 2 (where the line number is 1-based) will result in this error if you're using Node 12:

> TypeError: Line must be greater than or equal to 1, got -1

That's because of this line: https://github.com/vitejs/vite/blob/b204bcb6430bdff085269b036ca6503e354f3d50/packages/vite/src/node/ssr/ssrStacktrace.ts#L27

In Node 12, stack traces are accurate, as though the anonymous function wrapper didn't exist:

```js
const fn = new Function(`throw new Error('nope');n//# sourceURL=test.js`);
fn();

// in Node 12
// Uncaught Error: nope
//    at eval (test.js:1:7)

// in Node 13 and later
// Uncaught Error: nope
//    at eval (test.js:3:7)
```

Because of that, subtracting 2 is unnecessary. But it _is_ necessary in 13 and later.

If the original _doesn't_ go through line 1 or 2, no error will be raised, but the sourcemapped stack trace will be incorrect.

